            <ArticleTitle>Iatrogenic submedial coronary artery intramural hematoma presenting subacutely.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>E128-31</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We report an unusual case of unstable angina resulting from a rare subacute submedial intramural hematoma within the mid-proximal segment of the left anterior descending coronary artery 3 days after successful coronary angioplasty and stenting. An additional stent was deployed to contain the hemorrhage with good angiographic and clinical results.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
